<!--Post: 5144--><!--Time: 1106925302-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5144"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tippy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tippy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 28, 2005 - 7:15 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->This morning on KWCH Channel 12, out of Wichita, a psychologist, being interviewed suggested that BTK was dying and that these last few months of communication are his &#34;end game&#34;, his way of releasing the momentos that serial killers accumulate, little by little, in an effort to share the last vestiges of his crimes with the public. <BR> <BR>Another suggested that he really wants to be caught but just can&#39;t quite get up the nerve to say, &#34;Here I am, come get me...&#34; <BR> <BR>What do you think? <BR> <BR>Is this BTK&#39;s swan song? <BR> <BR>That scenario leaves me with more questions than answers.  If he is acting in a fatalistic manner - preparing, or clearing the way, for his own demise, will the PD take him alive? <BR> <BR>Have the police checked with the local cancer-treatment centers to advise the staff to be on the lookout for a patient that fits BTKs description? &#40;if they have any idea what that is&#41; <BR> <BR>If the psychologist was on the right track - does the fact that two drops occuring so closely together suggest that BTK&#39;s health has taken a distinct turn for the worst? <BR> <BR>Is he in a race against time at this point? <BR> <BR>What drives a serial killer who has defied the assumptions of the experts? One who quit killing when they said it was not possible?   <BR> <BR>The last postcard to KAKE embodied a tone one would not think a serial killer would use.  He questions them as to their knowledge of a previous drop, graciously, asks them kindly to verify it, and then thanks them. <BR> <BR>Out of character? <BR> <BR>Facing one&#39;s own mortality can bring out the best - or the worst - in a person.   <BR> <BR>Is he still playing the game?  Or is he ending it?  Slowly, regretfully, but completely? <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5144-->
<!--Post: 5152--><!--Time: 1106928128-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5152"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:Iwillc@tchu.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Catcher<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Catcher<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 28, 2005 - 8:02 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Interesting post Tippy.  IMO BTK came back to haunt the public, stir up some chaos and what have you, for his own narcissistic pleasure.  I do agree with Mr. Kheller&#39;s profile in that there was a catalyst to his reemergence into the spotlight, but I personally don&#39;t believe the terminal illness theory.  So to answer your inquisition, I think he&#39;s still playing the game.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5152-->
<!--Post: 5156--><!--Time: 1106930591-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5156"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jrl<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jrl<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 28, 2005 - 8:43 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think he&#39;s building up to some type of grand finale, whether it&#39;s terminal illness, confession, suicide, or another murder...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5156-->
<!--Post: 5158--><!--Time: 1106931184-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5158"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Devbost<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Devbost<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 28, 2005 - 8:53 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;m not convinced of the terminal illness angle. A possibility, of course, but impossible to know with very much certainty. It&#39;s obvious that he can still get around, as evidenced by the drop sites. I doubt that he&#39;d be taking the chance of being seen if he were not able to get in and out of his drops sites very quickly and with a minimum of visibility. <BR> <BR>I have reached the opinion that BTK is now retired from killing for whatever reason. If we&#39;ve got his birth year pegged correctly, then he&#39;d be getting up there in years by now, and he would have lost a step or two. It&#39;s possible that he&#39;s simply grown too old to be an effective killer, he realizes this, and has chosen to start communicating again for the attention it provides. <BR> <BR>His crimes were about control. And if he is indeed retired, then what better way to reassert some of that control than by reemerging after 18 years of silence to instill fear once more into the community?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5158-->
<!--Post: 5162--><!--Time: 1106931803-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5162"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 28, 2005 - 9:03 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I Posted this on the profile-thred but noone have reponded/read? it, so I´ll post it hear as well: <BR> <BR>What if BTK has a &#34;higher&#34; common motive with all the killings, a motive &#34;above&#34; the sadistic sexual plessaure he gets from the actual killings? &#40;wich no doubt was a huge part of his killings&#41;  <BR>Meaning that the killing of the victim in it self is just the &#34;tool&#34; to fullfill his motive &#40;goal&#41;.  <BR> <BR>And that the items he took from the victims was symbols that in the end would tell the story of his &#34;higher&#34; motive.  <BR> <BR>Remember he wrote &#34;you guess the victims and the motive&#34;  <BR> <BR>SO BTK choose his victims in advance making sure they fit in to the &#34;higher motive story&#34; wich is his REAL obsession/motivation.  <BR> <BR>After killing the victims he collect personal items from them in order to bulid a collection that &#34;pictures&#34; &#34;materialize&#34; his higer motive.  <BR> <BR>What he is doing now is passing over the &#34;collection&#34; bit by bit, in hope that socity and LE at som point get the message/picture of his &#34;higer motive&#34;.  <BR>Try to look at the items as a rebus that can reveal his choice of victims and his &#34;higer Motive&#34;  <BR> <BR>Now lets put the items, he has droped, in a row:  <BR> <BR>a watch  <BR>a pearl necklace  <BR>a doll &#40;not sure about this&#41;  <BR>a bundle of car keys &#40;not sure about this&#41;  <BR>an unidentified wrapped metallic object &#40;Fox package&#41;  <BR>poems about fantasies of the victims and the killings of them  <BR>Index of a serial killers &#34;story&#34;  <BR>puzzles &#40;words, mathematics?&#41;  <BR>Choices of drop off locations might also have a meaning to his &#34;higher motive&#34;  <BR>and probably more objects that we havent been informed about yet.  <BR> <BR>Besides this he have passed over items that I belive he droped to prove that he indeen was the killer of the victims:  <BR>pollaroid pictures of his victims  <BR>personal letters to LE, media and intended victims  <BR>sketches of the crime sceens  <BR>descriptions &#40;in words&#41; of the killings/crime-scenes  <BR>Driver licens of victims  <BR>several phone calls to media and to LE  <BR>and probably more info that we/I don´t know about yet.  <BR> <BR>SO IMO maybe BTK´s killings is, in som way, divided in two &#40;probably more&#41; levels/dimensions.  <BR>ONE level is the actual killings and the satisfaction he gets from them.  <BR>The other level/dimension is BTK´s &#34;higher motive&#34; which core could be:  <BR>&#34;idealistic &#40;philosophical? political? &#40;insane?&#41; fundamentalism&#34;  <BR>&#34;religious &#40;insane?&#41; fundamentalisme&#34;  <BR>&#34;personal &#40;insane?&#41;family issues&#34;  <BR>&#34;occult &#40;insane?&#41; fundamentalistic&#34;  <BR>ect ect.  <BR> <BR>This could mean that the victims had NO personal meaning to him AT ALL, insted they were all perfect &#34;bits&#34; and &#34;pices&#34; for the collection that in the end would provide socity with a shocking REVELATION of som sort.  <BR> <BR>Please brainstorm on this theorie and add more factual info on the lists.  <BR> <BR>I´m completely awear of that I might be totaly off on this, but I choose to share anyway.  <BR>And please remeber english is NOT my first language so PLEASE bear over with me.  <BR> <BR>thanks...skov<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5162-->
<!--Post: 5180--><!--Time: 1106939237-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5180"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 28, 2005 - 11:07 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->In his first letter &#40;Otero letter&#41; he wanted to make a point of correcting the 3 suspects the police had that were claiming responsibility for his crimes. <BR> <BR>He wanted credit. <BR> <BR> <BR>However he knows of many other unsolved murders in the Wichita area and he knows that there is wide speculation about whether he committed them or not. <BR> <BR>By just placing the #8 drop where he did it adds to the speculation about those cases and adds to the fear of the public because it widens the area of known BTK sites. <BR> <BR>All of this accomplished without claiming another murder. <BR> <BR>He wouldn&#39;t claim one that he didn&#39;t commit but not claiming while getting closer to some of them is an easy way to create fear and bring attention to himself... <BR> <BR>Master plan or just a means to his end game...??? <BR> <BR>If he didn&#39;t commit any of the murders in the Northern area... IMO he reads this board...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5180-->
<!--Post: 5181--><!--Time: 1106940263-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5181"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Essevi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Essevi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 28, 2005 - 11:24 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Without knowing what was put inside of the cereal box, we have no way of knowing if he claimed another unsolved murder. Whatever was inside that box, I sure wish I knew! Do you think LE will ever tell us?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5181-->
<!--Post: 5183--><!--Time: 1106940902-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5183"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Devbost<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Devbost<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 28, 2005 - 11:35 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><b><i>Without knowing what was put inside of the cereal box, we have no way of knowing if he claimed another unsolved murder.</i></b> <BR> <BR>We&#39;ll know more if he is ever caught. If the police conclude that he is responsible for another unsolved, unattributed murder, I&#39;m very sure that they would release that information to the public.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5183-->
<!--Post: 5189--><!--Time: 1106943941-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5189"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 28, 2005 - 12:25 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><i>&#34;By just placing the #8 drop where he did it adds to the speculation about those cases and adds to the fear of the public because it widens the area of known BTK sites.&#34;</i> Q, you put it better in one sentence than I attempted to in ten paragraphs.  <BR> <BR>Ess: if anything about an additional murder&#40;s&#41; were in the box, I think LE will say so when they think the time is right. The story is too big; if LE keeps mum, I think the press will have something to say. <BR> <BR>Dev: <i>&#34;His crimes were about control. And if he is indeed retired, then what better way to reassert some of that control than by reemerging after 18 years of silence to instill fear once more into the community?&#34;</i> I think that&#39;s extremely insightful and it makes sense through and through. &#40;BTW, sorry for past nonsense; peace?&#41;. One thing about the chronic illness. This is only a general thought. I always assumed cancer, or something requiring BTK being bedridden. As you say, this isn&#39;t the case and maybe this means that the idea of some sort of severe emotional trauma is more likely the cause for BTK&#39;s actions the past ten months. If so, I see the death of a relative, sister or mother  maybe. A <i>brother</i> perhaps?  <BR> <BR>One more thing about illness. If there is an MD, PA, RN or the like please correct me if I make a mistake on this, but what if the terminal illness is AIDS? It&#39;s possible there are too many variables for AIDS to be the case, I&#39;m not sure. For example, in 1986 a co-worker who was a chemist and was somewhat openly gay came to work on a Friday, looked happy, was joking, etc. Sunday, two days later, he had died from complications caused by the AIDS virus. But I&#39;ve also heard of AIDS patients being bedridden for weeks and weeks before passing away from AIDS.  Is AIDS too complicated to predict? <BR> <BR>Keeping along the AIDS guess, BTK did mention prostitutes but it&#39;s difficult to believe BTK about many things. I bring up prostitutes as I don&#39;t see other high-risk factors with BTK such as IV drugs and whatnot. I don&#39;t think BTK was gay although the Otero scene had two males and, well we know about the scene. Perhaps that crime scene indicates latent homosexuality? I still see BTK as heterosexual. Just speculating about all of this as I&#39;m frankly baffled about an end game. Great thread, Tippy.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5189-->
<!--Post: 5196--><!--Time: 1106947686-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5196"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 28, 2005 - 1:28 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I hope BTK didn&#39;t get the idea for the box from the movie <i>Se7en</i>. The general idea, I mean, a cereal box wouldn&#39;t work. Then again, movies are fantasy and BTK is fantasy-driven...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5196-->
<!--Post: 5201--><!--Time: 1106949129-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5201"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tippy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tippy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 28, 2005 - 1:52 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Catcher - if, as you say, he is still &#39;playing the game&#39; does his gameplan still include killing?  Do you think the psychologist was wrong about the &#39;relinquishing of momentos&#39; as a sign of &#40;at least&#41; some sort of change? <BR> <BR>Jrl - you bring suicide into the equation.  It strikes me &#40;perhaps wrongly&#41; that suicide may, indeed, be an option for one who exhibited such a need to &#39;control&#39; death.  On his terms, so to say. <BR> <BR>Dev - I totally agree that his crimes were about control.  What I find inconsistent is the giving up of his tokens.  I have to wonder why he does not simply write - and describe the killings - something that would still garner the attention - while keeping his prizes.  To me - that indicates some sort of a &#39;change of heart&#39;.  But, I&#39;m no criminologist. <BR> <BR>Skov - I think your theory is a real possibility.  Perhaps &#40;to BTK&#41; if he can &#39;share&#39; his trophies with us - he can open himself to us.  Maybe he can present himself as more acceptable, in his mind.  I have wondered if he ever longs for approval.  Ever wants to be understood.  Justified.  Perhaps, little by little, over a period of time, he feels he can &#39;win hearts&#39;.  One year ago - I would say that was crazy - but today, I see that BTK&#39;s messages are actually polarizing people.  They are begining to identify with him on some level.  Our interest is piqued.  I have been watching a phenomena develop whereby people are actually begining to portray the PD as the &#34;bad guys&#34;.  I try to watch myself in that area, since I don&#39;t like the way law enforcement is operating - but at the same time incompetence is not equivical to being a cold-blooded murderer.   <BR> <BR>Q - I am not so sure he didn&#39;t claim another murder - but I suppose we will have to wait on that.  I wonder if his &#39;rural&#39; drops are simply because he felt it was more inconspicuous.   <BR> <BR>Essevi - I think the PD will eventually tell us if BTK is linked conclusively to another murder, but outside of that - we may never know much.  I&#39;m not so sure that the public really needs more puzzels and poetry, especially if they are devised to confuse and detract.  I hope, if physical evidence is in the drops, that they will notify us.  But, other than that - they must be getting deluged with calls they can&#39;t possibly track down - and probably over false information - leading away, instead of, towards BTK.  Just my thoughts, though. <BR> <BR>George - I agree that LE will have to be forthcoming about something, I just hope it actually has substance this time. <BR> <BR>The AIDS scenario you bring up is very interesting.  I&#39;m not informed at all about that - but I would like to be.  It seems that I heard that an AIDS patient usually dies from something else - something he/she contracts that, because of AIDS, their system can not fight off.  But I could be way off base with that assumption.   <BR> <BR>How long are those who are infected living these days?  What are the medical needs? <BR> <BR>I believe there are free AIDS clinics that distribute the medications and that purchasing them otherwise is cost-prohibitive. <BR> <BR>I would really like someone to fill us in on that aspect.  You bring up some excellent points. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5201-->
<!--Post: 5203--><!--Time: 1106949219-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5203"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Devbost<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Devbost<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 28, 2005 - 1:53 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><b><i>&#40;BTW, sorry for past nonsense; peace?&#41;</i></b> <BR> <BR>Did you say something to me on another thread that you feel you have to apologize for? I must have missed it; this forum is so busy that it&#39;s not possible for me to catch everything. <BR> <BR>So since I have no idea what you&#39;re talking about, and because I&#39;m easy that way, OK and ditto on the peace thing. <IMG SRC="http://www.catchbtk.com/discus/clipart/happy.gif" ALT=":-&#41;" BORDER=0> <BR> <BR><b><i>Is AIDS too complicated to predict?</i></b> <BR> <BR>AIDS is very much a matter of how a certain person responds to it. Some people get sapped very quickly. Others can hang on with little or no outward appearance of sickness for 15 years or more. And there&#39;s everything in between. It&#39;s impossible to say if this is what is happening with BTK, or what his prognosis is if you&#39;re right. <BR> <BR><b><i>Perhaps that crime scene indicates latent homosexuality? I still see BTK as heterosexual.</i></b> <BR> <BR>That&#39;s probably a good question for Mike Kelleher.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5203-->
<!--Post: 5204--><!--Time: 1106949373-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5204"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 28, 2005 - 1:56 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Tippy: My point is that he doesn&#39;t have to claim another Murder to get the attention he craves... even if he did commit more. <BR> <BR>Of course he may have claimed or suggested he did in the evidence we don&#39;t get to see... just don&#39;t know...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5204-->
<!--Post: 5206--><!--Time: 1106949875-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5206"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Stealth<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Stealth<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 28, 2005 - 2:04 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->People that are going to kill themselves give their prize possessions away. That&#39;s why the psy folks are saying he&#39;s dying or he&#39;s going to off himself...His age range is ripe for prostate cancer, so that can&#39;t be discounted... <BR> <BR>Wichita doesn&#39;t exactly seem real terrified at this point to me.  Some people will always be scared of anything, but I am not seening panic in the streets.  Larry at KAKE was almost funny about BTK being a long time viewer and asking him to call. <BR> <BR>I am guessing he is treating the station like he treats most people, that&#39;s why he never got caught. <BR> <BR>He seems to be enjoying entertaining people.  But his actions say he is begging to be caught, perhaps it is subconscious.  He always played the odds but now he is defying them with frequency of actions.  He&#39;s got a lot of cops with a lot of tools on his ass and he keeps giving them chances. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5206-->
<!--Post: 5209--><!--Time: 1106951201-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5209"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Devbost<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Devbost<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 28, 2005 - 2:26 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><b><i>What I find inconsistent is the giving up of his tokens. I have to wonder why he does not simply write - and describe the killings - something that would still garner the attention - while keeping his prizes. To me - that indicates some sort of a &#39;change of heart&#39;.</i></b> <BR> <BR>You&#39;ve caused me to have one of those Hmmmm moments where I go back and reevaluate the logical frame I&#39;m using to think about the case. <BR> <BR>We&#39;ve all been operating under the assumption that these murders are major events in BTK&#39;s own consciousness. <BR> <BR>But what if they aren&#39;t, really? <BR> <BR>In our society, there is a common set of life events that most people share and which are major landmarks on the timeline of one&#39;s life. Graduation from college. Marriage. Birth of first child. These are events which for most have powerful emotional resonance, and souvenirs from these events are items which we generally avoid parting with. I have no practical reason for doing it, but I still have my cap and gown. My mom still has the baby shoes my dad had bronzed. <BR> <BR>Then there are those life events which we remember fondly, but which do not hold as great an emotional memory. That really fun trip to Hawaii, for instance, or the time you got to see Michael Crawford as the Phantom in New York. When you start cleaning out the garage, you may have a moment where you pause before tossing out the tiki doll you got, or the musty of Phantom of the Opera T-shirt. But nonetheless, you send them off to Goodwill. <BR> <BR>What if the souvenirs that BTK collected from the crime scenes are more like the tiki doll to him than the baby shoes? What if the murders are to him no more significant than the nice vacation or the really great concert? <BR> <BR>Mike Kelleher&#39;s profile indicates that BTK almost assuredly has his own photographs from the crime scenes, and that he&#39;s probably gone to the trouble of digitizing his collection. It&#39;s not like he doesn&#39;t still have mementos, and it&#39;s more of a statement to send Nancy Fox&#39;s actual driver&#39;s license in a communication than it is to send a photocopy, isn&#39;t it? <BR> <BR>This is not to debunk the notion that some significant event has occured in his life that has caused him to make contact. There&#39;s got to be some explanation for coming out of the woodwork after an 18-year silence, and I&#39;m willing to bet that it isn&#39;t boredom. <BR> <BR>I could be totally wrong about all of this. Heck, I probably <b>am</b> totally wrong. But it&#39;s another facet of the psychological portrait to consider. Perhaps someone else will read this and have a useful Hmmmm moment of their own.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5209-->
<!--Post: 5212--><!--Time: 1106951754-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5212"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:Iwillc@tchu.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Catcher<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Catcher<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 28, 2005 - 2:35 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Tippy, good question.  I believe there are a few facets stimulating the recent treasure hunt. <BR> <BR>1.  I think BTK for whatever reason, has become lonely and depressed.  In retrospect of better days, his demented mind brought him back to the killing stage of his life. In order to emulate the feelings that once fulfilled him, he made some sacrifices by releasing his treasures. <BR> <BR>It&#39;s like the Buddhist way of thinking - It&#39;s not until you&#39;ve lost everything, that you&#39;re free to do anything. <BR> <BR>In a way, I feel that BTK is both punishing himself, and freeing himself by ridding the treasures/evidence; this is his aging epiphany. <BR> <BR>2.  BTK enjoys taunting the public and police, he feels UBER powerful.  He wants to be something bigger and better than any other historically significant killer.  In order to fulfill this fantasy, he does what no other SK has been able to, he returns his tokens; maybe some, maybe all.  I think that in moments of lucidity, he is capable of rationalizing this enough to actually do it.  It&#39;s operational risk management: <BR>Identify hazards, mitigate risks, and take action <BR>Accept no unnecessary risks <BR>Make risk decisions at the appropriate level <BR>Accept risks when benefits outweigh costs <BR> <BR>I think BTK accepts the risks and loss of the treasure hunt game, for the end means will be the greatest benefit of all.     <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5212-->
<!--Post: 5216--><!--Time: 1106951976-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5216"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:Iwillc@tchu.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Catcher<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Catcher<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 28, 2005 - 2:39 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->AMEN Dev!  Great post!  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5216-->
<!--Post: 5241--><!--Time: 1106969662-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5241"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 28, 2005 - 7:34 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Freudian Psychoanalysis can be useful in assessing the importance of the murders in the life of the BTK Strangler. At the conscious level the murders do not appear important to the unknown subject. The unknown subject would project a facade of respectability. He would cherish rites of passages, such as graduating from college and marriage. Unconsciously, the murders are important to him. The murders satisfy the id or his basic desires. Preparing to murder, the modus operandi and executing victims compensate for a feeling he is not fully enjoying life. He may have an unsatisfactory sexual relationship with his wife or former wife or resorts to masturbation to provide relief in the absence of a companion. It seems the unknown subject has a strong superego. It prevents his violent sexual fantasies escaping from his unconscious in relationships with family or friends.  <BR> <BR>It seems the murders have preoccupied his mind at certain times. The murders would have dominated the life of the BTK Strangler from 1973 until 1979. The 25 years of silence could be interpeted as a period where the unknown subject did not focus on the murders. He could have attempted to live normally and occasionally murder when the id became too strong. A significant event in his life prompted him to correspond with the police during the last year. It could have been a divorce or the death of a relative. I do not believe he is suffering from a life threatening illness. His strong superego allows him to undertake some risky behavior without incriminating him. It seems likely he will continue to correspond with the police. The unknown subject enjoys taunting the police, public, the media and dominating the news in Wichita and occasionally on a national stage. He could become enraged when Beattie&#39;s book is published. However, his meticulous approach will ensure he is not apprehended.      <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5241-->
<!--Post: 5256--><!--Time: 1106983230-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5256"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 28, 2005 - 11:20 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Tippy, an emotional trauma seems more probable now but if BTK has a terminal illness AIDS would be a likely guess. You are correct; no one dies from AIDS, they die from complications which their immune system can&#39;t fight off. Pneumonia is common but there are also AIDS-related heart attacks and so forth. The last I heard at the lab was a dormancy period of a few weeks up to eighteen months, but this is old information <b>and newer data must be introduced and verified by a physician or other proper authority.</b> I also believe you&#39;re correct about the clinics. The &#34;cocktail&#34; treatment is expensive. The current price should be provided or estimated by the proper authority. I believe that state by state, provided funds differ. Federal funding is not politically popular but some money does come from the Feds, the amount I don&#39;t know.  <BR> <BR>Magic Johnson, formerly of the Los Angeles Lakers basketball team has had AIDS for quite some time but then his athleticism and relative youth are possibly a large reason for this. He also has the resources to acquire world class, cutting-edge treatment. There have been other drugs since AZT and with treatment the average AIDS patient has a longer average life span than twenty years ago and often a substantially longer life span when compared to twenty years ago. I know how to read medical books, papers and so forth but am not qualified to answer anything but the most general questions concerning AIDS. There must be an AMA related link with the newest information available, with said information being valid as it would be written by epidemiologists, researchers, and so forth. I&#39;d look right now but my esophageal erosion came back with a vengeance after a welcome absence and it feels like I have molten steel in my entire torso; I need to go purchase a large bottle of antacid. I agree with you, AIDS may be the only terminal condition which BTK might have, if he is indeed terminal. <BR> <BR>An emotional shock or trauma looks like the best bet at this point concerning BTK&#39;s re-emergence. However, the AIDS information is too important to bypass, at least in some encapsulated form. I have got to go get some Maalox - physical pain is an incredible motivator. Quickly on BTK and suicide. BTK, I think, knows some will regard his actions, especially the original of the Fox driver&#39;s license being &#34;returned,&#34; as suicidal ideation or an approximation thereof. This may or may not be the case. My opinion is that BTK long ago &#40;pre- Wegerle revelation&#41; has suicide as a contingency plan. That he still taunts and must be in complete control of his dropoffs stymies any significant suicidal intent, in my layman&#39;s opinion. He&#39;s still having fun. I have also seen little to convince me that BTK is suffering depression. <BR> <BR>I&#39;m afraid it&#39;s possible that, while we may be witnessing a prolonged coda, the end result may be BTK slipping right back into the shadows, as others have noted on this board. From the Wegerle information last March until right now, I don&#39;t believe BTK was ever motivated by altruism one whit. Nor do I believe a sudden finding of religion on BTK&#39;s part or his sending the parcels a form of atonement. BTK is a complete sociopath and couldn&#39;t care less about his victims, or by extension society, which is also his victim. I realize how grim that scenario seems and I&#39;d like to think BTK suddenly grew a conscience, but if we&#39;re here to post our honest thoughts, I just don&#39;t see it. There are evil people in this world and BTK is one of them. I hope to God I am wrong. Gotta run along now. Stellar thread, Tippy! Excuse typos I&#39;m in a rush.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5256-->
<!--Post: 5257--><!--Time: 1106983652-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5257"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dpinva<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dpinva<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 28, 2005 - 11:27 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->It seems to me that things with BTK are moving much faster and I feel that they are speeding up to something happening pretty soon that will end the chase. I am begining to sense that for some reason BTK is running on a ticking clock. He is giving away what must be for him valuable heirlooms and is getting more open and more sloppy, possibly in my view intentionally.  <BR>I can&#39;t help thinking that BTK is struggling with his own mortality in a very intimate and immediate way. There are a number of possibilites: <BR>1&#41; BTK is terminally ill and knows he will die soon and is laying out a path of evidence to insure that he gets the proper credit for his BTK &#34;work&#34; after he has died,  <BR>2&#41; BTK has irrevocably chosen to committ suicide for some reason &#40;again a terminal disease is possible here, but perhaps one that is either much earlier in its development or takes a longer progression, such as AIDS or ALS&#41; and is again seeking to lay a path of evidence for Law Enforcement to follow after his death,  <BR>3&#41; BTK feels that he is about to be discovered and that the mechanism of that discovery is beyond his control, such as a relative or document he forgot about that he has realized will reveal him, he has been visited by WPD or other Law Enforcement and knows that they know and it is a matter of time, <BR>4&#41;he genuinely has had a profound change in his life and beliefs and wants to give it up - repent and get right with his higher power &#40;whoever he believes God to be&#41; and turn himself in. He might also want to turn himself in for other reasons that are known, and quite possibly only make any sense what so ever, to him and him alone that have great spiritual or otehr kind of significane that is basic to his existence, <BR>5&#41;he genuinely wants to turn himself in because he is simply exhausted from having lived with his actions for all of this time without being caught and punished. History is replete with people who &#34;got away with it&#34; only to have to confess it later so that they could live with themselves in peace at last. Even if it seems that he truly enjoys the &#34;game&#34; of the chase that we are seeing at the moment, and I am quite sure that he does to some degree, at the end of the day he wants to get caught of only to be at peace with himself. I am not saying he wants to do any of these options for others, as BTK is if anything preternatally selfish, but his desire to do it for himself - &#34;it&#34; in this context being whatever he is actually trying to accomplish - could overwhelm any other considerations. <BR>Whatever the reason, I have the gut sense of a pastor here that something it going on deep inside of BTK that needs a specific, concrete resolution of some kind. BTK&#39;s communications have gotten more much frequent, more brazen and less organized, and far more personal than before, as seen in BTK&#39;s giving up trophies from murders, which historically serial killers have virtually never done for any reason until and except for BTK this year. One way or another, this whole thing will be over fairly soon. BTK will die, be taken into custody, disappear back into the ether &#40;although I don&#39;t see this as very likely at all&#41; or go out in a blaze of glory, hollywood fantasy style ending &#40;as we all know fantasy is an important element of BTK&#39;s logic&#41;.  <BR>Whatever the reasons, I am pretty confident that before a whole lot of 2005 has passed the world will know who BTK is and will know the details of his crimes, and it will prbably be, if not initiated, at least enabled by BTK himself. BTK may not be alive after its over or maybe he will be, but if it goes however he has in mind, either way he will be the talk of the town. Lots of talk. In lots of towns. He will be in a sense immortal then whether he is dead or alive. I think that in the most basic core of BTK&#39;s heart and soul, it is that immortaility that matters the most. Time will tell....... <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5257-->
<!--Post: 5262--><!--Time: 1106985235-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5262"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 28, 2005 - 11:53 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->He&#39;s been back at this taunting game since last March.  <BR>He don&#39;t seem in no big hurry to me.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
