<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5266"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Topsailgrl<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Topsailgrl<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 29, 2005 - 5:26 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->What better way for BTK to gain immortality than to stir the public again and then die quietly without ever being caught?  <BR> <BR>I do believe that he has killed in the 18 years that he was &#34;silent&#34;. He states in one of his communications, &#34;<i>You guess the motive and the victims.</i>&#34;. He also states in that same communication that, &#34;<i>I will be like that until the urge hits me again.</i>&#34; I do not believe that he has not had that urge in the 18 years that we did not hear from him.  <BR> <BR>End game is very plausible. Weather it be certain upcoming demise from disease or suicide. Maybe also up coming prison sentence? Has anyone thought of that maybe. He may be charged with a murder that does not appear to be a BTK murder and know that he is getting ready to go into the penal system for the remainder of his life. He can sit back in prison and read about himself from time to time, knowing that he has &#34;stirred&#34; the pot again and will live on in infamy.  <BR> <BR>I do not believe he wants to be caught. He knows that caught alive, he will have no control over his life. And  we know that control means so very much to him. I honestly believe that he wants gain that immortality by people reading about him a 100 years from now still trying to figure out who he is. And what better way to do that than to tease and rouse people before you vanish into thin air? <BR> <BR>At the same time, I believe he is enjoying this immensely. Hopefully that enjoyment is what is going to get him caught. He seems to have great control but after all he is still human and urges can be great. He is loving reading peoples thoughts about him. He didn&#39;t have that privilege back in the 70&#39;s and early 80&#39;s. I bet this has changed things for him. Gives him the opportunity to enjoy the tease and clues a little longer and on a more personal level. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5266-->
<!--Post: 5268--><!--Time: 1107015131-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5268"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Clairevoient<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Clairevoient<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 29, 2005 - 8:12 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Tippy, I am enjoying your thoughtful posts. <BR> <BR>Catcher, Debvost, George, Q, excellent threadwork. <BR> <BR>See what Who&#39;sYourFloydW? had to say to B_ _T_ _ _K® on this subject. <BR> <BR>Posted on Friday, January 28, 2005 - 11:58 pm: <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
