<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5281"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lilymarie<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lilymarie<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 29, 2005 - 10:29 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Tippy - your interesting post and the subsequent thread is one of the best on this site. I am going to take a little time to digest your original point - the tokens and items meaning less to him than we have taken for granted. Also, loved your analogy about vacation souvineers vs cherished memories. Nice idea and great writing. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
